Native outlines for segmentation layers in the 2-D views (not applied).

ngplatform draws outlines today with an image layer that reads the same
labels (src/engine/outline_shader.ts).  This patch lets the segmentation
layer do it itself: a new layer setting `outlineWidth` (JSON key
"outlineWidth"; 0, the default, fills as now), which keeps hover
highlighting, selected and visible segments, equivalences and stated
colours exactly as the filled drawing, and needs no second layer.

It uses getDataValueAt, vChunkPosition and uChunkDataSize, which every
chunk format (uncompressed and compressed_segmentation) defines for the
slice-view shader.  Untested against the fork's own tests; written against
the fork as of this branch.  Apply in the fork with:
    patch -p1 < segmentation-outlines.patch

